## Role execution guidance (you author hypotheses; you run NO evaluations)
- exploit: take the strongest-mechanism near-miss verdicts (e.g. cov/ symbol with
  pf>1 or high ic that did not clear the gate) and propose a refined symbol x cov
  combination with a sharper mechanism and pre-registered kill/promote conditions.
- falsifier: do NOT chase the leaderboard. Identify the most load-bearing
  mechanism claim behind a frontier/near-miss result and author a proposal that
  would DISPROVE it (e.g. the same covariate on a symbol where the mechanism
  predicts it should FAIL). Publish finding_type=challenge via share_finding.
- bridge: propose a symbol that combines two non-redundant covariate families
  (e.g. CCL positioning x rsi_state), with an explicit combined mechanism and a
  reasoning chain for why the interaction adds edge over each alone.
- anti_mainline: your proposals are FORBIDDEN from using the dominant families
  (see anti_mainline contract above if present, else the families already on the
  frontier). Cover the neglected families: oi, ccl, volume-related (nvi, vor),
  calendar_cyclical, structure (crack_spread, basis, vwap).

## End-of-generation checklist
1. Every hypothesis written as a JSON file under the canonical proposals tree
   {{ results_dir | default("<run_dir>/results") }}/gen_{{ gen_id | default(0) }}/{{ peer_id | default("peer") }}/proposals/<symbol>_<covariate>.json
   Use a heredoc or Write tool. Do NOT use scripts/praxist_ws/ (delete-guard blocked).
2. Every proposal has: mechanism (>=40 chars), symbol_fit, predicted_direction,
   kill_condition, promote_condition, and an ACTIVE covariate from the pool menu.
3. Every hypothesis/insight/challenge also published via share_finding with
   extra={symbol, covariate, mechanism, proposal_id}. Publish >=2-3 this generation.
4. New-indicator ideas (not in the pool) use new_cov_<name>.json with
   cov_override=null and a new_covariate object (these go to the host backlog).
5. Done means: proposal files landed in the canonical proposals tree (not your
   workspace or /tmp) — that is the only place the supervisor reads.
